==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|prenuptial|agreement}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[legal]] [[document]], signed by both [[parties]] before [[marriage]], stating the legal [[claim]]s on each other's [[estate]] upon a [[subsequent]] [[divorce]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Tamar Lewin|title=Among Nuptial Agreements, Post- Has Now Joined Pre-|magazine=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2001/07/07/us/among-nuptial-agreements-post-has-now-joined-pre.html|date=07-07-2001|passage=Not so long ago, '''prenuptial agreements''' raised eyebrows. What hope was there for a marriage, the thinking went, if even before the wedding the couple were specifying who gets what in case of divorce?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Phillip Galanes|title=My Boyfriend Wants a Prenup. Can I Say No?|magazine=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/10/style/prenup-resentment.html|date=10-05-2023|passage=Last week, he said we should get married and that he wants a '''prenuptial agreement'''.}}

